{"type":"standard","title":"Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q6273609","titles":{"canonical":"Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins","normalized":"Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins</span></span>"},"pageid":38339991,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/JKTphoto_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-JKTphoto_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/JKTphoto_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1340,"height":1786},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1375880645","tid":"3814ef83-b516-11f1-90cb-33610b715564","timestamp":"2026-09-20T17:10:46Z","description":"American politician (born 1989)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jonathan_Kreiss-Tomkins"}},"extract":"Jonathan S. Kreiss-Tomkins, also known as JKT, is an American politician who was a member of the Alaska House of Representatives from 2013 to 2023. A Democrat, he represented the state's 35th district, which encompasses many Southeast island communities, including Hoonah, Sitka, Kake, Klawock, Craig, Angoon, and Petersburg. Kreiss-Tomkins is the Democratic nominee in the 2026 Alaska gubernatorial election.","extract_html":"<p><b>Jonathan S. Kreiss-Tomkins</b>, also known as <b>JKT</b>, is an American politician who was a member of the Alaska House of Representatives from 2013 to 2023. A Democrat, he represented the state's 35th district, which encompasses many Southeast island communities, including Hoonah, Sitka, Kake, Klawock, Craig, Angoon, and Petersburg. Kreiss-Tomkins is the Democratic nominee in the 2026 Alaska gubernatorial election.</p>"}